Export format icons

Aseprite uses unmodified artwork from the official Aseprite v1.1.6 repository.
SVG uses the official W3C SVG Logo without the W3C wordmark.
See each asset's subdirectory for its source, attribution, and license.

PNG, JPEG/JPG, WebP, ORA, TIFF, BMP, PSD, indexed PNG, GIF, and PNG sprite-sheet
export use text badges naming the actual file format. These are original UI
labels, not third-party software logos or claims of an official format logo.

Adobe's Photoshop application icon is not bundled. The published Adobe icon
policy does not grant permission to use application icons in a third-party
application: https://www.adobe.com/legal/permissions/icons-web-logos.html
OpenRaster is an interchange format, rather than one particular application:
https://www.openraster.org/
